Verse 2:
[Bb]When through [Eb]the woods
[Eb]And [Bb]forest [F]glades [F7]I [Bb]wander
[Bb]And hear the birds [Eb]sing sweetly in the trees
[Eb][Bb]When [F]I [F7]look [Bb]down
[Bb]From [Eb]lofty [Bb]mountain grandeur
[Bb]And see [F]the brook [F7]and feel [Bb]the gentle breeze

Verse 3:
[Bb]And when [Eb]I think
[Eb]That [Bb]God [F]His [F7]Son [Bb]not sparing
[Bb]Sent Him to die I [Eb]scarce can take it in
[Eb][Bb]That [F]on [F7]the [Bb]Cross
[Bb]My [Eb]burden [Bb]gladly bearing
[Bb]He bled [F]and died [F7]to take [Bb]away my sin.

Verse 4:
[Bb]When Christ [Eb]shall come
[Eb][Bb]With [F]shouts [F7]of [Bb]acclamation
[Bb]And take [Eb]me home
[Eb]What [Bb]joy [F]shall [F7]fill [Bb]my heart
[Bb]Then [Eb]I [Bb]shall bow
[Bb][F]In [F7]humble [Bb]adoration
[Bb]And [Eb]then [Bb]proclaim
[Bb]"My God, [F7]how great [Bb]Thou art!"
